01:02:38,181 --> 01:02:44,181
Lyle, Lyle, Crocodile is a 2022 American live-action animated musical fantasy comedy film
directed by Will Speck and Josh Gordon from a screenplay by William Davies.

14
01:07:27,272 --> 01:07:33,272
Produced by Columbia Pictures and distributed by Sony Pictures Releasing, it is an adaptation of the
children's story of the same name and its predecessor The House on East 88th Street by Bernard Waber.

15
01:12:16,363 --> 01:12:22,363
The plot focuses on a family who moves to New York City, where their struggling son befriends an
anthropomorphic crocodile, Lyle, who can communicate verbally only by singing.

16
01:17:05,454 --> 01:17:11,454
The son tries to protect Lyle from the rest of the world.

17
01:21:54,545 --> 01:22:00,545
The film stars Shawn Mendes as Lyle's singing voice, alongside Javier Bardem,
Constance Wu, Winslow Fegley, Scoot McNairy, and Brett Gelman.

18
01:26:43,636 --> 01:26:49,636
Lyle, Lyle, Crocodile was released in the United States
on October 7, 2022, by Columbia Pictures.

19
01:31:32,727 --> 01:31:38,727
The film received generally mixed reviews from critics and grossed $111 million.

20
01:36:21,818 --> 01:36:27,818
The film explores themes of crocodile, musical, based on
children's book, outsider, live action and animation.

21
